concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 Subsection 20A(4)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-4 ;
    values:originalText "Omit all the words from and including “if” to and including “the order” substitute:  if the court is satisfied that:  (a) there are not reasonable grounds to suspect that the person’s *total wealth exceeds by $100,000 or more the value of the person’s *wealth that was *lawfully acquired; or  (b) it is not in the public interest to make the order." ;
    skos:definition "Omit all the words from and including “if” to and including “the order” substitute:  if the court is satisfied that:  (a) there are not reasonable grounds to suspect that the person’s *total wealth exceeds by $100,000 or more the value of the person’s *wealth that was *lawfully acquired; or  (b) it is not in the public interest to make the order."@en ;
