concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-10 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 After subsection 45A(3)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-10 ;
    values:originalText "Insert: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006  Unexplained wealth  Schedule 1  No. 6, 2015 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other Measures) Act 2015  Restraining orders made after application for unexplained wealth order  (3A) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force if:  (a) the restraining order was made at the same time as or after an application for an *unexplained wealth order is made in relation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates; and  (b) the court refuses to make either:  (i) a *preliminary unexplained wealth order in connection with the application for the unexplained wealth order; or  (ii) the unexplained wealth order itself; and  (c) one of the following applies:  (i) the time for an appeal against the refusal has expired without an appeal being lodged;  (ii) an appeal against the refusal has lapsed;  (iii) an appeal against the refusal has been dismissed and finally disposed of.  (3B) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force if:  (a) the restraining order was made at the same time as or after an application for an *unexplained wealth order is made in relation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates; and  (b) the court makes the unexplained wealth order (whether before or after the restraining order was made or applied for); and  (c) either:  (i) the unexplained wealth order is complied with; or  (ii) an appeal against the unexplained wealth order has been upheld and finally disposed of." ;
    skos:definition "Insert: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006  Unexplained wealth  Schedule 1  No. 6, 2015 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other Measures) Act 2015  Restraining orders made after application for unexplained wealth order  (3A) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force if:  (a) the restraining order was made at the same time as or after an application for an *unexplained wealth order is made in relation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates; and  (b) the court refuses to make either:  (i) a *preliminary unexplained wealth order in connection with the application for the unexplained wealth order; or  (ii) the unexplained wealth order itself; and  (c) one of the following applies:  (i) the time for an appeal against the refusal has expired without an appeal being lodged;  (ii) an appeal against the refusal has lapsed;  (iii) an appeal against the refusal has been dismissed and finally disposed of.  (3B) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force if:  (a) the restraining order was made at the same time as or after an application for an *unexplained wealth order is made in relation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates; and  (b) the court makes the unexplained wealth order (whether before or after the restraining order was made or applied for); and  (c) either:  (i) the unexplained wealth order is complied with; or  (ii) an appeal against the unexplained wealth order has been upheld and finally disposed of."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1c5f057e65947d69d5e667d8861b6f0a3208bfb73fedbe35d03a6ee8abccc552" ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-10-ss-3a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-10-ss-3b ;
