    skos:definition "(3A) A *restraining order made under section 20A ceases to be in force if:  (a) the restraining order was made at the same time as or after an application for an *unexplained wealth order is made in relation to the *suspect to whom the restraining order relates; and  (b) the court refuses to make either:  (i) a *preliminary unexplained wealth order in connection with the application for the unexplained wealth order; or  (ii) the unexplained wealth order itself; and  (c) one of the following applies:  (i) the time for an appeal against the refusal has expired without an appeal being lodged;  (ii) an appeal against the refusal has lapsed;  (iii) an appeal against the refusal has been dismissed and finally disposed of."@en ;
