concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-19 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "19 Subsection 179E(4)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-19 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (4) To avoid doubt:  (a) when considering whether to make an order under subsection (1), the court may have regard to information not included in the application; and  (b) the court may make an order under subsection (1) in relation to a person even if the person failed to appear as required by the *preliminary unexplained wealth order. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006  Schedule 1  Unexplained wealth  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other Measures) Act 2015 No. 6, 2015" ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (4) To avoid doubt:  (a) when considering whether to make an order under subsection (1), the court may have regard to information not included in the application; and  (b) the court may make an order under subsection (1) in relation to a person even if the person failed to appear as required by the *preliminary unexplained wealth order. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006  Schedule 1  Unexplained wealth  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other Measures) Act 2015 No. 6, 2015"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9367e7f6db46edcd4b780c86ccc616bc6968a5e729b42df4372a7584b1f5ecae" ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court may consider information not included in application when making an order under subsection (1)." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
