    cml:conclusionText "(3) The charge:  (a) is subject to every *encumbrance on the property (other than an encumbrance in which the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a) has an *interest) that came into existence before the charge and that would, apart from this subsection, have priority over the charge; and" ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-1-sec-179sa-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "179SA(3) Charge on property subject to restraining order" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The charge:  (a) is subject to every *encumbrance on the property (other than an encumbrance in which the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a) has an *interest) that came into existence before the charge and that would, apart from this subsection, have priority over the charge; and  (b) has priority over all other encumbrances; and  (c) subject to subsection (2), is not affected by any change of ownership of the property." ;
    cof:pageNumber "13"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-179sa-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179SA(4) Charge on property subject to restraining order"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-179sa-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Subsection 73(2) of the Personal Property Securities Act 2009 applies to the charge (to the extent, if any, to which that Act applies in relation to the property charged). Note: The effect of this subsection is that the priority between the charge and a security interest in the property to which the Personal Property Securities Act 2009 applies is to be determined in accordance with this Act rather than the Personal Property Securities Act 2009." ;
    skos:definition "(4) Subsection 73(2) of the Personal Property Securities Act 2009 applies to the charge (to the extent, if any, to which that Act applies in relation to the property charged). Note: The effect of this subsection is that the priority between the charge and a security interest in the property to which the Personal Property Securities Act 2009 applies is to be determined in accordance with this Act rather than the Personal Property Securities Act 2009."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "abef81c3efd582d7f37312f0b9918672e16f8db5d55e86c4a97be2bd3155b195" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-179sa ;
    cof:pageNumber "13"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Priority between charge and security interest determined by this Act." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
