concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-179sb a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179SB Charges may be registered"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-179sb ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a charge is created by section 179SA on property of a particular kind; and  (b) the provisions of any law of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory provide for the registration of title to, or charges over, property of that kind; the *Official Trustee or the *responsible authority for the *unexplained wealth order or *restraining order referred to in that section may cause the charge so created to be registered under the provisions of that law.  (2) A person who purchases or otherwise acquires an *interest in the property after the registration of the charge is taken, for the ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006  Unexplained wealth  Schedule 1  No. 6, 2015 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other Measures) Act 2015  purposes of paragraph 179SA(2)(d), to have notice of the charge at the time of the purchase or acquisition.  (3) In this section: registration of a charge on a particular kind of personal property within the meaning of the Personal Property Securities Act 2009 includes the registration of data in relation to that kind of property for the purposes of paragraph 148(c) of that Act. Note: The Personal Property Securities Act 2009 provides for the registration of such data only if regulations are made for the purposes of paragraph 148(c) of that Act." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a charge is created by section 179SA on property of a particular kind; and  (b) the provisions of any law of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory provide for the registration of title to, or charges over, property of that kind; the *Official Trustee or the *responsible authority for the *unexplained wealth order or *restraining order referred to in that section may cause the charge so created to be registered under the provisions of that law.  (2) A person who purchases or otherwise acquires an *interest in the property after the registration of the charge is taken, for the ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00006  Unexplained wealth  Schedule 1  No. 6, 2015 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Unexplained Wealth and Other Measures) Act 2015  purposes of paragraph 179SA(2)(d), to have notice of the charge at the time of the purchase or acquisition.  (3) In this section: registration of a charge on a particular kind of personal property within the meaning of the Personal Property Securities Act 2009 includes the registration of data in relation to that kind of property for the purposes of paragraph 148(c) of that Act. Note: The Personal Property Securities Act 2009 provides for the registration of such data only if regulations are made for the purposes of paragraph 148(c) of that Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5a9b8c833bb35c39e791433699ed51050e211dc776e9bcfd424cd368f8de4c3c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-179sb-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-179sb-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-unexplained-wealth-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-1-sec-179sb-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
